# PET/AL/PE High Barrier Packaging Structure

PET/AL/PE is a high-barrier flexible packaging structure often considered when products need stronger protection against moisture, oxygen, light and aroma loss.

It may be used for coffee packaging, powder packaging, seasoning packaging, retort pouch packaging, pet food packaging and other products that require higher barrier performance.

Official website: https://gdhspack.com

## What Is PET/AL/PE?

PET/AL/PE usually means:

- PET outer printing layer
- AL aluminum foil barrier layer
- PE inner heat sealing layer

PET supports printing appearance and structure.

AL aluminum foil provides strong barrier performance against light, oxygen and moisture.

PE provides heat sealing performance.

The final material specification should be confirmed according to product type, filling weight, shelf life requirement, storage condition and packing method.

## Common Applications

PET/AL/PE may be used for:

- Coffee packaging
- Powder packaging
- Seasoning packaging
- High-barrier snack packaging
- Pet food packaging
- Retort pouch packaging
- Food packaging roll film
- Flat bottom pouches
- Stand up zipper pouches
- Kraft paper laminated bags

For products with sterilization, pasteurization or retort processing requirements, the material structure should be reviewed more carefully.

## Why Use Aluminum Foil?

Aluminum foil is often used when packaging needs stronger barrier performance.

Possible reasons include:

- Strong light barrier
- Strong oxygen barrier
- Strong moisture barrier
- Better aroma protection
- Longer shelf life support
- Better protection for sensitive food products

However, aluminum foil structures may increase cost and may affect flexibility, recyclability or machine compatibility depending on the project.

## PET/AL/PE vs PET/VMPET/PE

| Item | PET/VMPET/PE | PET/AL/PE |
|---|---|---|
| Barrier Layer | Metallized PET | Aluminum foil |
| Light Barrier | Good | Stronger |
| Oxygen Barrier | Good | Stronger |
| Moisture Barrier | Good | Stronger |
| Cost | Usually lower | Usually higher |
| Flexibility | Usually better | Depends on foil thickness and structure |
| Common Uses | Coffee, snacks, dry food | High-barrier food, aroma-sensitive products, retort-related projects |

The final choice should be based on product testing, shelf life requirement and packaging performance needs.

